{
  "description": "Shared test vectors for the sandbox call key and the signed execution proof. A second implementation must reproduce every value. Generated with an independent implementation of the recipe (ADR 'Recipe of the call_key'); the Rust tests check them.",
  "callKey": {
    "recipe": "Each field is written as <tag length>:<tag>=<value length>:<value>| (lengths are byte counts in decimal ASCII), after a first field `domain`; the digest is lowercase hex SHA-256; the key is `sandbox.exec#<hex>`. call: domain sandbox.call.v1, tenant, run, node, create, exec (the two fingerprints as hex text). create: domain sandbox.create.v1, profile, limits (JSON), network (JSON), ttlMs, inputs (count) then each input (JSON), env (count) then for each envName, envRef. exec: domain sandbox.exec.v2, argc, each arg, then cwdSet (0, or 1 followed by cwd), then stdinSet (always 0: standard input is refused under approval, so no approved call carries any). Numbers are decimal ASCII; structured values are compact JSON of plain structs in declaration order.",
